    "negative_clarification": "Not credit-claiming occurs when a senator discusses issues, policies, or outcomes without explicitly or implicitly attributing them to their own actions. This includes general statements of support, criticism, or advocacy that do not link a specific positive result to their personal involvement. It also includes commemorative statements, expressions of concern, or discussions of broader policy without claiming responsibility for an outcome.",
